## Verification method

The Release "'`--selftest` uses isolated notes under the build output; it bypasses the production hotkey and tray. Internal show-to-focus timing ends when the retained editor reports keyboard focus. It does not measure physical hotkey-to-compositor-paint latency. The M3 fixture is loaded into the actual editor and laid out; this is scripted evidence, not a physical checkbox-click or visual-quality approval.

## Accepted Avalonia limits

AvaloniaEdit uses natural font line height, without a leading setting. Fenced panels cannot add per-line inner text padding. The stock folding margin retains its box/guide geometry. This task leaves the opaque rectangular shell and its existing always-on-top behavior intact. Other DPI settings and physical mouse behavior need a desktop check.
